{"seq":2,"slug":"remote-collaboration","title":"远程协作沟通英语","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/programmer-english/communication-english/remote-collaboration","wordCount":1388,"readingTime":6,"html":"<h1 id=\"远程协作沟通英语\">远程协作沟通英语</h1><h2 id=\"核心概念\">核心概念</h2><p>远程协作的英语沟通发生在<strong>没有语气、表情和即时澄清</strong>的环境里。&quot;差不多说清&quot;在这里会直接变成误解，因此核心原则是<strong>过度沟通好过沟通不足</strong>，且每条消息都要自带结构。</p>\n<p>三条可操作的约定：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>结构化</strong>：Slack 消息遵循&quot;TL;DR 在前，细节在后&quot;；邮件用 Subject + 目的句 + 正文 + 行动项</li>\n<li><strong>显式表达不确定性</strong>：<code>I&#39;m not 100% sure</code> / <code>Let me recap</code> 比默默猜测更专业</li>\n<li><strong>标注紧急程度</strong>：<code>Not urgent</code> / <code>Time-sensitive</code> / <code>🚨 blocking the release</code> 让接收方正确排期</li>\n</ul>\n<pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"graph\" data-source=\"graph TD&#10;    A[远程协作英语] --&gt; B[结构化消息]&#10;    A --&gt; C[显式表达不确定性]&#10;    A --&gt; D[标注紧急程度]&#10;    A --&gt; E[困难对话处理]&#10;    B --&gt; F[TL;DR 在前 细节在后]&#10;    B --&gt; G[邮件 Subject 目的 正文 行动项]&#10;    C --&gt; H[我不确定 / 请澄清 / 我复述确认]&#10;    D --&gt; I[Not urgent / Time-sensitive / blocking]&#10;    E --&gt; J[推回截止日期 报坏消息 拒绝请求]&#10;    F --&gt; K[跨时区异步一次读懂]&#10;    I --&gt; K&#10;    J --&gt; K\">graph TD\n    A[远程协作英语] --&gt; B[结构化消息]\n    A --&gt; C[显式表达不确定性]\n    A --&gt; D[标注紧急程度]\n    A --&gt; E[困难对话处理]\n    B --&gt; F[TL;DR 在前 细节在后]\n    B --&gt; G[邮件 Subject 目的 正文 行动项]\n    C --&gt; H[我不确定 / 请澄清 / 我复述确认]\n    D --&gt; I[Not urgent / Time-sensitive / blocking]\n    E --&gt; J[推回截止日期 报坏消息 拒绝请求]\n    F --&gt; K[跨时区异步一次读懂]\n    I --&gt; K\n    J --&gt; K</pre><p>在这些基础上，AI 工具成为&quot;虚拟同事&quot;后又新增了一类语境：如何用英语向人类同事描述 AI 失败、如何分享 prompt、以及如何与团队对齐 AI 使用边界。其底层逻辑不变——<strong>给可触发的复现、给具体证据、给明确的下一步</strong>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"slack-消息的结构化表达\">Slack 消息的结构化表达</h2><p>Slack 是远程团队最核心的异步沟通工具。与面对面交流不同，文字消息没有语气和表情的辅助，因此需要更有结构和更加精确的表达。</p>\n<h3 id=\"消息结构原则\">消息结构原则</h3><p>一条好的 Slack 技术消息应当遵循 &quot;TL;DR 在前，细节在后&quot; 的结构：</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"[一句话摘要/请求]&#10;&#10;[背景或细节]&#10;&#10;[具体问题或行动请求]\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>[一句话摘要/请求]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>[背景或细节]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>[具体问题或行动请求]</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"请求帮助的模板\">请求帮助的模板</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"Hey team — I&#39;m hitting a weird issue with the auth service.&#10;&#10;Getting a 401 on the /refresh endpoint even though the refresh token&#10;is valid (verified in the database). Started happening after yesterday&#39;s&#10;deploy.&#10;&#10;Has anyone seen this before? Or could someone point me to the relevant&#10;code? I&#39;ve looked at auth-service/src/middleware but couldn&#39;t find the&#10;token validation logic.\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Hey team — I'm hitting a weird issue with the auth service.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Getting a 401 on the /refresh endpoint even though the refresh token</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>is valid (verified in the database). Started happening after yesterday's</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>deploy.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Has anyone seen this before? Or could someone point me to the relevant</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>code? I've looked at auth-service/src/middleware but couldn't find the</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>token validation logic.</span></span></code></pre></div><p>关键要素分析：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>第一行点明问题性质</li>\n<li>中间描述现象和已做的排查</li>\n<li>最后提出具体请求</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"汇报状态更新\">汇报状态更新</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"📋 Quick update on the search feature (JIRA-789):&#10;&#10;✅ Completed:&#10;- Elasticsearch index schema designed&#10;- Data pipeline from Postgres to ES working in staging&#10;&#10;🔄 In progress:&#10;- Query builder implementation (should be done by EOD)&#10;&#10;⚠️ Heads up:&#10;- The synonym dictionary needs content team input before we can finalize&#10;  relevance tuning. I&#39;ll reach out to @sarah today.&#10;&#10;ETA for PR: Thursday\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>📋 Quick update on the search feature (JIRA-789):</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>✅ Completed:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Elasticsearch index schema designed</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Data pipeline from Postgres to ES working in staging</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>🔄 In progress:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Query builder implementation (should be done by EOD)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>⚠️ Heads up:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- The synonym dictionary needs content team input before we can finalize</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  relevance tuning. I'll reach out to @sarah today.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>ETA for PR: Thursday</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"提出技术建议\">提出技术建议</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"Thinking about our caching strategy for the product catalog —&#10;&#10;Currently we&#39;re cache-aside with a 10-min TTL, but I&#39;ve noticed cache&#10;miss rates are ~35% during traffic spikes.&#10;&#10;Proposal: Switch to write-through caching with event-based invalidation.&#10;This would give us:&#10;- Near-zero cache miss rate for product data&#10;- Guaranteed consistency (no stale data)&#10;- ~40% reduction in DB read load&#10;&#10;Trade-off: Slightly higher write latency (~15ms per write).&#10;&#10;WDYT? Worth a spike? I can put together a design doc if folks are interested.\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Thinking about our caching strategy for the product catalog —</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Currently we're cache-aside with a 10-min TTL, but I've noticed cache</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>miss rates are ~35% during traffic spikes.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Proposal: Switch to write-through caching with event-based invalidation.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>This would give us:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Near-zero cache miss rate for product data</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Guaranteed consistency (no stale data)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- ~40% reduction in DB read load</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Trade-off: Slightly higher write latency (~15ms per write).</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>WDYT? Worth a spike? I can put together a design doc if folks are interested.</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"常用-slack-表达\">常用 Slack 表达</h3><p><strong>开头语</strong>：</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"&quot;Quick question about...&quot;&#10;&quot;Heads up — ...&quot;&#10;&quot;FYI: ...&quot;&#10;&quot;PSA: ...&quot;  (Public Service Announcement)&#10;&quot;Friendly reminder: ...&quot;&#10;&quot;Just a thought — ...&quot;\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>\"Quick question about...\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Heads up — ...\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"FYI: ...\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"PSA: ...\"  (Public Service Announcement)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Friendly reminder: ...\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Just a thought — ...\"</span></span></code></pre></div><p><strong>请求回应</strong>：</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"&quot;Could someone take a look at...?&quot;&#10;&quot;Any thoughts on this?&quot;&#10;&quot;@here — need eyes on a production issue&quot;&#10;&quot;Does anyone have context on...?&quot;&#10;&quot;Who&#39;s the right person to ask about...?&quot;\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>\"Could someone take a look at...?\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Any thoughts on this?\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"@here — need eyes on a production issue\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Does anyone have context on...?\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Who's the right person to ask about...?\"</span></span></code></pre></div><p><strong>确认与回应</strong>：</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"&quot;Got it, thanks!&quot;&#10;&quot;Makes sense — I&#39;ll proceed with that approach.&quot;&#10;&quot;Acknowledged. I&#39;ll take care of it.&quot;&#10;&quot;Thanks for the heads up. I&#39;ll keep an eye on it.&quot;&#10;&quot;Noted. Let me know if anything changes.&quot;\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>\"Got it, thanks!\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Makes sense — I'll proceed with that approach.\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Acknowledged. I'll take care of it.\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Thanks for the heads up. I'll keep an eye on it.\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Noted. Let me know if anything changes.\"</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id=\"技术邮件写作\">技术邮件写作</h2><p>邮件适合需要正式记录、涉及多方的沟通场景。与 Slack 相比，邮件更注重格式完整性和语气的专业性。</p>\n<h3 id=\"技术邮件结构\">技术邮件结构</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"Subject: [Clear, actionable subject line]&#10;&#10;Hi [name / team],&#10;&#10;[Opening — 1 sentence context or purpose]&#10;&#10;[Body — details, organized with bullets or paragraphs]&#10;&#10;[Closing — clear next steps or call to action]&#10;&#10;Best,&#10;[Your name]\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Subject: [Clear, actionable subject line]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Hi [name / team],</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>[Opening — 1 sentence context or purpose]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>[Body — details, organized with bullets or paragraphs]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>[Closing — clear next steps or call to action]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Best,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>[Your name]</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"常见邮件场景模板\">常见邮件场景模板</h3><p><strong>请求技术评审</strong>：</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"Subject: RFC review request: Event-driven notification system&#10;&#10;Hi Backend Team,&#10;&#10;I&#39;ve drafted an RFC for migrating our notification system from&#10;polling to event-driven architecture. The document covers the&#10;proposed Kafka topic design, consumer group strategy, and rollback plan.&#10;&#10;RFC link: [link]&#10;&#10;Key decisions I&#39;d appreciate feedback on:&#10;1. Topic partitioning strategy (Section 3.2)&#10;2. Dead letter queue handling (Section 4.1)&#10;3. Migration timeline (Section 6)&#10;&#10;If possible, I&#39;d like to get feedback by Friday EOD so we can&#10;discuss in Monday&#39;s architecture review.&#10;&#10;Thanks,&#10;Alex\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Subject: RFC review request: Event-driven notification system</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Hi Backend Team,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>I've drafted an RFC for migrating our notification system from</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>polling to event-driven architecture. The document covers the</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>proposed Kafka topic design, consumer group strategy, and rollback plan.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>RFC link: [link]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Key decisions I'd appreciate feedback on:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>1. Topic partitioning strategy (Section 3.2)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>2. Dead letter queue handling (Section 4.1)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>3. Migration timeline (Section 6)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>If possible, I'd like to get feedback by Friday EOD so we can</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>discuss in Monday's architecture review.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Thanks,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Alex</span></span></code></pre></div><p><strong>通知技术变更</strong>：</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"Subject: [Action Required] API v1 deprecation — migration deadline March 15&#10;&#10;Hi API consumers,&#10;&#10;As announced in January, API v1 will be fully deprecated on March 15, 2026.&#10;After this date, all v1 endpoints will return 410 Gone.&#10;&#10;What you need to do:&#10;- Migrate all API calls to v2 endpoints&#10;- Update authentication to use OAuth 2.0 (v1 API keys will stop working)&#10;- Review the migration guide: [link]&#10;&#10;Breaking changes in v2:&#10;- Pagination uses cursor-based instead of offset-based&#10;- Date fields now return ISO 8601 format&#10;- Rate limits reduced from 1000 to 500 req/min (with burst support)&#10;&#10;If you need help migrating or have concerns about the timeline,&#10;please reply to this email or reach out in #api-migration on Slack.&#10;&#10;Best,&#10;Platform Team\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Subject: [Action Required] API v1 deprecation — migration deadline March 15</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Hi API consumers,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>As announced in January, API v1 will be fully deprecated on March 15, 2026.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>After this date, all v1 endpoints will return 410 Gone.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>What you need to do:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Migrate all API calls to v2 endpoints</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Update authentication to use OAuth 2.0 (v1 API keys will stop working)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Review the migration guide: [link]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Breaking changes in v2:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Pagination uses cursor-based instead of offset-based</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Date fields now return ISO 8601 format</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Rate limits reduced from 1000 to 500 req/min (with burst support)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>If you need help migrating or have concerns about the timeline,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>please reply to this email or reach out in #api-migration on Slack.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Best,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Platform Team</span></span></code></pre></div><p><strong>事后报告（Post-mortem）通知</strong>：</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"Subject: Post-mortem: Payment service outage (May 3, 14:22-15:47 UTC)&#10;&#10;Hi all,&#10;&#10;Sharing the post-mortem for yesterday&#39;s payment service incident.&#10;&#10;Impact: 23% of payment attempts failed for 85 minutes.&#10;Root cause: Connection pool exhaustion due to a slow downstream query.&#10;Resolution: Increased pool size + added circuit breaker for the slow endpoint.&#10;&#10;Full post-mortem: [link]&#10;&#10;Action items (owners assigned in the doc):&#10;- Add connection pool metrics to our dashboard (Platform - this week)&#10;- Implement circuit breaker pattern for all external calls (Backend - Sprint 12)&#10;- Add load test scenario for connection exhaustion (QA - Sprint 12)&#10;&#10;Please review and add any missing context. We&#39;ll discuss in&#10;Thursday&#39;s engineering all-hands.&#10;&#10;Thanks,&#10;On-call team\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Subject: Post-mortem: Payment service outage (May 3, 14:22-15:47 UTC)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Hi all,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Sharing the post-mortem for yesterday's payment service incident.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Impact: 23% of payment attempts failed for 85 minutes.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Root cause: Connection pool exhaustion due to a slow downstream query.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Resolution: Increased pool size + added circuit breaker for the slow endpoint.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Full post-mortem: [link]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Action items (owners assigned in the doc):</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Add connection pool metrics to our dashboard (Platform - this week)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Implement circuit breaker pattern for all external calls (Backend - Sprint 12)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Add load test scenario for connection exhaustion (QA - Sprint 12)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Please review and add any missing context. We'll discuss in</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Thursday's engineering all-hands.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Thanks,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>On-call team</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id=\"跨时区协作策略\">跨时区协作策略</h2><h3 id=\"时区感知表达\">时区感知表达</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"&quot;I&#39;ll have this ready by EOD my time (UTC+8), which is your morning.&quot;&#10;&quot;Can we find a time that works across all three time zones?&quot;&#10;&quot;I&#39;ll leave async comments on the PR since you&#39;ll be offline when I review.&quot;&#10;&quot;Sending this before I sign off — no rush, just FYI for your morning.&quot;&#10;&quot;I&#39;ll be online during your afternoon (my evening) if you need to sync.&quot;\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>\"I'll have this ready by EOD my time (UTC+8), which is your morning.\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Can we find a time that works across all three time zones?\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"I'll leave async comments on the PR since you'll be offline when I review.\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Sending this before I sign off — no rush, just FYI for your morning.\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"I'll be online during your afternoon (my evening) if you need to sync.\"</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"异步优先的沟通习惯\">异步优先的沟通习惯</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"&quot;No need to respond today — just leaving this here for when you&#39;re back.&quot;&#10;&quot;Recorded a Loom video explaining the architecture decision: [link]&quot;&#10;&quot;I&#39;ve documented my thinking in the RFC. Please leave comments async.&quot;&#10;&quot;Updated the ticket with my findings. Take a look when you get a chance.&quot;&#10;&quot;Left detailed comments on the PR. Happy to hop on a call if anything&#10; is unclear, otherwise async is fine.&quot;\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>\"No need to respond today — just leaving this here for when you're back.\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Recorded a Loom video explaining the architecture decision: [link]\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"I've documented my thinking in the RFC. Please leave comments async.\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Updated the ticket with my findings. Take a look when you get a chance.\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Left detailed comments on the PR. Happy to hop on a call if anything</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span> is unclear, otherwise async is fine.\"</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"紧急程度表达\">紧急程度表达</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"&quot;Not urgent — just when you get a chance.&quot;&#10;&quot;No rush on this.&quot;&#10;&quot;Time-sensitive: need a decision by EOD Thursday.&quot;&#10;&quot;🚨 This is blocking the release — need help ASAP.&quot;&#10;&quot;Whenever you have a moment — no pressure.&quot;&#10;&quot;High priority but not time-critical. This sprint is fine.&quot;\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>\"Not urgent — just when you get a chance.\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"No rush on this.\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Time-sensitive: need a decision by EOD Thursday.\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"🚨 This is blocking the release — need help ASAP.\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Whenever you have a moment — no pressure.\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"High priority but not time-critical. This sprint is fine.\"</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id=\"表达不确定性与寻求澄清\">表达不确定性与寻求澄清</h2><p>在远程沟通中，及时表达困惑比默默猜测更专业：</p>\n<h3 id=\"表达不确定\">表达不确定</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"&quot;I&#39;m not 100% sure about this, but...&quot;&#10;&quot;My understanding is X — can someone confirm?&quot;&#10;&quot;I might be wrong here, but I think...&quot;&#10;&quot;Correct me if I&#39;m mistaken, but...&quot;&#10;&quot;I&#39;m fuzzy on the details of...&quot;\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>\"I'm not 100% sure about this, but...\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"My understanding is X — can someone confirm?\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"I might be wrong here, but I think...\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Correct me if I'm mistaken, but...\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"I'm fuzzy on the details of...\"</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"请求澄清\">请求澄清</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"&quot;Just to clarify — are you saying that...?&quot;&#10;&quot;Could you elaborate on what you mean by...?&quot;&#10;&quot;I want to make sure I understand correctly: ...&quot;&#10;&quot;When you say X, do you mean A or B?&quot;&#10;&quot;Sorry, I didn&#39;t quite catch that. Could you rephrase?&quot;\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>\"Just to clarify — are you saying that...?\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Could you elaborate on what you mean by...?\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"I want to make sure I understand correctly: ...\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"When you say X, do you mean A or B?\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Sorry, I didn't quite catch that. Could you rephrase?\"</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"确认理解\">确认理解</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"&quot;So if I&#39;m understanding correctly, the plan is...&quot;&#10;&quot;Let me recap to make sure we&#39;re aligned: ...&quot;&#10;&quot;Just to confirm — my action item is to...&quot;&#10;&quot;So the decision is to go with option B. Is that right?&quot;&#10;&quot;I&#39;ll proceed with X unless I hear otherwise.&quot;\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>\"So if I'm understanding correctly, the plan is...\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Let me recap to make sure we're aligned: ...\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Just to confirm — my action item is to...\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"So the decision is to go with option B. Is that right?\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"I'll proceed with X unless I hear otherwise.\"</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id=\"困难对话的处理\">困难对话的处理</h2><h3 id=\"推回不合理的截止日期\">推回不合理的截止日期</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"&quot;I appreciate the urgency, but I have concerns about the timeline.&#10;Here&#39;s why: [specific technical reasons]. Could we discuss a phased&#10;approach where we deliver the core functionality first?&quot;&#10;&#10;&quot;I want to set realistic expectations — given the complexity and our&#10;current workload, I&#39;d estimate [timeframe]. Would it help if I&#10;outlined what we could deliver incrementally?&quot;\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>\"I appreciate the urgency, but I have concerns about the timeline.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Here's why: [specific technical reasons]. Could we discuss a phased</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>approach where we deliver the core functionality first?\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"I want to set realistic expectations — given the complexity and our</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>current workload, I'd estimate [timeframe]. Would it help if I</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>outlined what we could deliver incrementally?\"</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"报告坏消息\">报告坏消息</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"&quot;I wanted to flag a risk early: the integration is more complex than&#10;we initially estimated. Based on what I&#39;ve learned this week, I think&#10;we&#39;ll need an additional sprint. Here&#39;s what I&#39;ve found: [details].&quot;&#10;&#10;&quot;Unfortunately, I discovered a blocker that will impact our timeline.&#10;I&#39;ve already started exploring alternatives: [options].&quot;\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>\"I wanted to flag a risk early: the integration is more complex than</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>we initially estimated. Based on what I've learned this week, I think</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>we'll need an additional sprint. Here's what I've found: [details].\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"Unfortunately, I discovered a blocker that will impact our timeline.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>I've already started exploring alternatives: [options].\"</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"拒绝请求\">拒绝请求</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"&quot;I&#39;d love to help, but my plate is full with [current priority].&#10;Could we revisit this next sprint?&quot;&#10;&#10;&quot;That&#39;s an interesting idea, but it&#39;s outside the scope of this sprint.&#10;Can we add it to the backlog for consideration?&quot;&#10;&#10;&quot;I don&#39;t think I&#39;m the right person for this — you might want to&#10;check with the platform team.&quot;\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>\"I'd love to help, but my plate is full with [current priority].</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Could we revisit this next sprint?\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"That's an interesting idea, but it's outside the scope of this sprint.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Can we add it to the backlog for consideration?\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"I don't think I'm the right person for this — you might want to</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>check with the platform team.\"</span></span></code></pre></div><p>远程协作的英语沟通核心原则是：<strong>过度沟通好过沟通不足</strong>。宁可多说一句确认，也不要因为怕麻烦而让误解发酵。同时，尊重他人的时间——消息要结构化，请求要具体，紧急程度要明确标注。</p>\n<h2 id=\"ai-工具协作场景的英语\">AI 工具协作场景的英语</h2><p>当团队中 LLM 工具（Cursor / Copilot / Claude Code / 内部 AI 助手）成为&quot;虚拟同事&quot;，远程沟通新增了一类语境：<strong>与 AI 协作时如何用英语描述、如何向人类同事沟通 AI 工具的输入输出</strong>。</p>\n<h3 id=\"在-slack-描述-ai-失败的英语\">在 Slack 描述 AI 失败的英语</h3><p>当 AI 工具帮你时出错，跟同事说明常见场景：</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"# Bad — 不可复现&#10;&quot;AI keeps generating wrong code, anyone else?&quot;&#10;&#10;# Good — 给同事可触发的复现&#10;&quot;FYI — Claude Code&#39;s edit tool failed on /web/apps/english/server.ts&#10;when I asked it to extract the auth middleware. It tried to edit&#10;the same lines twice. Workaround: split into two prompts. Anyone&#10;seeing this elsewhere?&quot;\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span># Bad — 不可复现</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"AI keeps generating wrong code, anyone else?\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span># Good — 给同事可触发的复现</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"FYI — Claude Code's edit tool failed on /web/apps/english/server.ts</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>when I asked it to extract the auth middleware. It tried to edit</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>the same lines twice. Workaround: split into two prompts. Anyone</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>seeing this elsewhere?\"</span></span></code></pre></div><p>模板：<strong>工具 + 文件 + 我让它做什么 + 它做错了什么 + 我的 workaround</strong>。和 bug report 5 段同构，只是把&quot;程序&quot;换成&quot;AI 工具&quot;。</p>\n<h3 id=\"描述-prompt-的英语\">描述 prompt 的英语</h3><p>跟同事分享 prompt 时，比直接贴 prompt 多一句<strong>意图说明</strong>：</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"Here&#39;s the prompt I use for generating PR descriptions — feel free to&#10;adapt. The constraint section (&quot;Use imperative mood&quot;, &quot;don&#39;t invent&#10;tests&quot;) is the part that mattered most; without it the output is&#10;much fluffier.&#10;&#10;[paste prompt]\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Here's the prompt I use for generating PR descriptions — feel free to</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>adapt. The constraint section (\"Use imperative mood\", \"don't invent</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>tests\") is the part that mattered most; without it the output is</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>much fluffier.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>[paste prompt]</span></span></code></pre></div><p>意图说明的句式：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>&quot;The key constraint is X — without it, the output is Y.&quot;</li>\n<li>&quot;I tried 3 versions; this one works because Z.&quot;</li>\n<li>&quot;Adjust the {variable} section for your context.&quot;</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"与-ai-队友-协作的边界沟通\">与 AI &quot;队友&quot;协作的边界沟通</h3><p>团队里有人用 AI 重度、有人不用，沟通中容易产生隐形冲突。常见场景与英语模板：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>场景</th>\n<th>模板</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>同事的 PR 看起来是 AI 生成的，质量有问题</td>\n<td>&quot;Hey, just a heads-up — section 3 of the PR reads like AI draft (e.g., &#39;leverages the power of&#39;). Could you double-check the implementation matches what&#39;s described?&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>同事问&quot;这是 AI 写的吗&quot;，但语气带审视</td>\n<td>&quot;Yes, drafted with AI then edited. The constraints / business logic are mine. Happy to walk through the parts I&#39;m less sure about.&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>想让团队对齐 AI 使用规范</td>\n<td>&quot;Should we add a brief section to CONTRIBUTING.md about AI-assisted PRs? I&#39;m thinking: disclose if used, human-verify before submit, no AI for review comments. Open to other suggestions.&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><strong>关键英语短语</strong>：<code>drafted with AI</code> / <code>AI-assisted</code> / <code>AI-augmented</code> 是社区当前主流措辞；避免 <code>AI-generated</code>（暗示零编辑）和 <code>written by AI</code>（容易引发&quot;那你做了什么&quot;质疑）。</p>\n<h3 id=\"跨时区-ai-的-异步加速-模式\">跨时区 + AI 的&quot;异步加速&quot;模式</h3><p>AI 让异步协作变得更高效：你下班前在 Slack 留 thread，同事用 AI 帮自己快速理解上下文。配套的英语句式：</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" data-lang=\"text\" data-code=\"# 留高质量异步消息（给 AI 容易理解的同事）&#10;&quot;## Context&#10;We need to decide whether to use Postgres LISTEN/NOTIFY or Redis pub/sub&#10;for the new notification service.&#10;&#10;## What I&#39;ve ruled out&#10;- Kafka: overkill at our scale (&lt; 1k events/sec)&#10;- WebSocket direct: lacks fanout&#10;&#10;## What&#39;s left&#10;- Postgres LISTEN/NOTIFY: simpler ops, tied to existing DB&#10;- Redis pub/sub: faster, adds Redis dependency&#10;&#10;## What I need from you&#10;Your read on whether we&#39;re OK adding Redis to ops surface.&#10;&#10;Not blocking; pick this up when you&#39;re online.&quot;\"><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span># 留高质量异步消息（给 AI 容易理解的同事）</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>\"## Context</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>We need to decide whether to use Postgres LISTEN/NOTIFY or Redis pub/sub</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>for the new notification service.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>## What I've ruled out</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Kafka: overkill at our scale (&#x3C; 1k events/sec)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- WebSocket direct: lacks fanout</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>## What's left</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Postgres LISTEN/NOTIFY: simpler ops, tied to existing DB</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>- Redis pub/sub: faster, adds Redis dependency</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>## What I need from you</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Your read on whether we're OK adding Redis to ops surface.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Not blocking; pick this up when you're online.\"</span></span></code></pre></div><p>这种结构化消息既方便人读，也方便同事用 AI 总结。&quot;Not blocking; pick this up when you&#39;re online&quot; 是地道的异步收尾句。</p>\n<h2 id=\"小结\">小结</h2><ul>\n<li>远程沟通没有语气与即时澄清，核心原则是&quot;过度沟通好过沟通不足&quot;，每条消息自带结构</li>\n<li>Slack 消息遵循&quot;TL;DR 在前，细节在后&quot;；请求帮助时把&quot;现象 + 已排查 + 具体请求&quot;说清</li>\n<li>邮件比 Slack 更正式：Subject 明确可行动，正文含目的句、要点与下一步</li>\n<li>跨时区协作要主动做时区感知表达，并养成异步优先的习惯</li>\n<li>显式表达不确定性（<code>I&#39;m not 100% sure</code> / <code>Let me recap</code>）比默默猜测更专业</li>\n<li>困难对话有三种模板：推回不合理截止日期（给技术理由 + 分阶段方案）、报告坏消息（早 flag 风险 + 给替代）、拒绝请求（说明当前优先级 + 给替代路径）</li>\n<li>紧急程度要明确标注：<code>Not urgent</code> / <code>Time-sensitive</code> / <code>🚨 blocking the release</code></li>\n<li>AI 成为&quot;虚拟同事&quot;后新增语境：用&quot;工具 + 文件 + 意图 + 错误 + workaround&quot;报告 AI 失败；分享 prompt 时补一句意图说明；用 <code>drafted with AI</code> 而非 <code>AI-generated</code> 描述协作方式</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"level":1,"text":"远程协作沟通英语","id":"远程协作沟通英语"},{"level":2,"text":"核心概念","id":"核心概念"},{"level":2,"text":"Slack 消息的结构化表达","id":"slack-消息的结构化表达"},{"level":3,"text":"消息结构原则","id":"消息结构原则"},{"level":3,"text":"请求帮助的模板","id":"请求帮助的模板"},{"level":3,"text":"汇报状态更新","id":"汇报状态更新"},{"level":3,"text":"提出技术建议","id":"提出技术建议"},{"level":3,"text":"常用 Slack 表达","id":"常用-slack-表达"},{"level":2,"text":"技术邮件写作","id":"技术邮件写作"},{"level":3,"text":"技术邮件结构","id":"技术邮件结构"},{"level":3,"text":"常见邮件场景模板","id":"常见邮件场景模板"},{"level":2,"text":"跨时区协作策略","id":"跨时区协作策略"},{"level":3,"text":"时区感知表达","id":"时区感知表达"},{"level":3,"text":"异步优先的沟通习惯","id":"异步优先的沟通习惯"},{"level":3,"text":"紧急程度表达","id":"紧急程度表达"},{"level":2,"text":"表达不确定性与寻求澄清","id":"表达不确定性与寻求澄清"},{"level":3,"text":"表达不确定","id":"表达不确定"},{"level":3,"text":"请求澄清","id":"请求澄清"},{"level":3,"text":"确认理解","id":"确认理解"},{"level":2,"text":"困难对话的处理","id":"困难对话的处理"},{"level":3,"text":"推回不合理的截止日期","id":"推回不合理的截止日期"},{"level":3,"text":"报告坏消息","id":"报告坏消息"},{"level":3,"text":"拒绝请求","id":"拒绝请求"},{"level":2,"text":"AI 工具协作场景的英语","id":"ai-工具协作场景的英语"},{"level":3,"text":"在 Slack 描述 AI 失败的英语","id":"在-slack-描述-ai-失败的英语"},{"level":3,"text":"描述 prompt 的英语","id":"描述-prompt-的英语"},{"level":3,"text":"与 AI \"队友\"协作的边界沟通","id":"与-ai-队友-协作的边界沟通"},{"level":3,"text":"跨时区 + AI 的\"异步加速\"模式","id":"跨时区-ai-的-异步加速-模式"},{"level":2,"text":"小结","id":"小结"}],"prev":{"title":"技术会议与站会英语","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/programmer-english/communication-english/meeting-standup-english"},"next":{"title":"技术演讲英语","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/programmer-english/communication-english/tech-talk-english"}}